        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Correct erroneous LargestContentfulPaint data I spotted:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Safari and Firefox do not support <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code></li>\n<li>Safari DOES support cross-origin render times.</li>\n<li>Chrome does support <code class=\"notranslate\">paintTime</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> but behind a flag (unflagging in Chrome 145!)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari does support cross-origin lcp render time but not <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> (tested on <a href=\"https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/lcp-cross-origin/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/lcp-cross-origin/</a>)<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198292-e3e64c66-0f96-4be1-97ce-351922bddcdf.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..dqT-HkaB_bUrgRtIUbXar_thkGdeljIrgQ8ki_3jwOo\"><img width=\"1583\" height=\"810\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198292-e3e64c66-0f96-4be1-97ce-351922bddcdf.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..dqT-HkaB_bUrgRtIUbXar_thkGdeljIrgQ8ki_3jwOo\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 810px;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Firefox gives null for <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code>:</strong></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198467-50acd617-cf85-4629-926a-607fbad2a6c9.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..sVgI7H4SkgokzLCuKaA8zY4U6b-8GwuSiz0A31YcbDo\"><img width=\"1481\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198467-50acd617-cf85-4629-926a-607fbad2a6c9.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..sVgI7H4SkgokzLCuKaA8zY4U6b-8GwuSiz0A31YcbDo\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 836px;\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Chrome 134 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">paintTime</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> when experimental web platform features are turned on:</strong></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198260-3a01c5c9-b8d3-4375-843c-1c8de9e90d9f.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..H7EGPibucaNHUXI4iKP3QyfEyUhQBYnkI4dS6XPKBQ8\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1162\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198260-3a01c5c9-b8d3-4375-843c-1c8de9e90d9f.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..H7EGPibucaNHUXI4iKP3QyfEyUhQBYnkI4dS6XPKBQ8\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1162px;\"></a>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28658",
            "title": "Misc LargestContentfulPaint updates",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-13T15:11:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-13T15:11:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 147 adds support for the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/counter-increment\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">counter-*</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/quotes\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">quotes</code></a> properties on the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::marker\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">::marker</code></a> pseudo-element. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2000404\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2000404</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a separate data point for <code class=\"notranslate\">counter-*</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">quotes</code>, as I thought some browsers may conceivably add support separately, and they feel like different concerns.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have created a test case at <a href=\"https://codepen.io/Chris-Mills/pen/yyOGdGJ?editors=1100\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codepen.io/Chris-Mills/pen/yyOGdGJ?editors=1100</a>. In testing, I found that the features:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Work in Firefox 147, but not 146</li>\n<li>Don't work in Chrome Canary or Safari technology preview.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28625",
            "title": "Firefox 147 supports `counter-*` and `quotes` properties on `::marker`",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-10T12:00:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T16:43:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/782446?u=b04ff20ddafb41870583859554c1e7c3180adca3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Added implementation URLs for Bun, Chrome and Node.js support.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28614",
            "title": "Add Temporal bugs for Bun + Node.js",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T17:30:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-08T14:11:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "simon04",
                "url": "https://github.com/simon04"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 supports WebGPU on on all macOS versions on apple silicon in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1993341\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1993341</a>.<br>\nPreviously it was only supported on Tahoe - I can't find a bug for that, but this issue stated that it was added for Tahoe in 145. It isn't supported on Linux. It isn't supported on macOS on Intel.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have updated the (partial) subfeatures in the 250+ places that support is recorded.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699234339\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42247\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42247/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42247\">mdn/content#42247</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28604",
            "title": "FF147 WebGPU supported on all apple silicon",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-15T01:10:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-08T03:40:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change addresses the dev-docs-needed requirement of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773681\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1773681</a> Enable showing \"Paste\" button for <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.clipboard.readText()</code> when called from Addons which don't have <code class=\"notranslate\">clipboardRead</code> permssion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In addition, it also corrects what appeared to be an erroneous copy paste of notes for the read methods to the write methods.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699868119\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42263\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42263/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42263\">mdn/content#42263</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587",
            "title": "Bug-1773681 updated navigator.clipboard read and write notes",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-08T19:17:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-05T18:14:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/939727?u=2e25f47c213a7e8f2e4e57ddd4ee59ba6601eae3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the new <code class=\"notranslate\">referencetarget</code> attribute to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;template&gt;</code> and property to the ShadowRoot API.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Explainer: <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md\">https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md</a></li>\n<li>HTML progress: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2592669740\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10707\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/issues/10707/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10707\">whatwg/html#10707</a></li>\n<li>WHATNOT progress: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3403461116\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11648\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/issues/11648/hovercard?comment_id=3293932780&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11648#issuecomment-3293932780\">whatwg/html#11648 (comment)</a></li>\n<li>Chrome implementation status: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188237101891584\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188237101891584</a></li>\n<li>Positive signal from Mozilla: <a href=\"https://mozilla.github.io/standards-positions/#1035\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mozilla.github.io/standards-positions/#1035</a></li>\n<li>Plans for WebKit implementation: <a href=\"https://blogs.igalia.com/mrego/solving-cross-root-aria-issues-in-shadow-dom/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://blogs.igalia.com/mrego/solving-cross-root-aria-issues-in-shadow-dom/</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28570",
